  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 91036662a85844eb162bdfbe2ea8ce9c, type: 3}
  m_Name: InternationalRules
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  displayName: International
  description: 10x10 draughts - flying kings, mandatory maximum capture, men can capture backward.
  longDescription: "<b>Basic Movement</b>\nDark Squares Only: pieces move diagonally on the 50 dark squares. Forward Only: regular pieces can only step one square diagonally forward.\n\n<b>Capture Mechanics</b>\nBackward Captures: regular pieces can jump backward to capture, even though they can't step backward normally. Mandatory Maximum: jumps are strictly mandatory, and you must choose the path that captures the most pieces, whether they're regular pieces or Kings. The No-Removal Rule: captured pieces stay on the board until your entire multi-jump turn is complete - you can't jump over the same piece twice.\n\n<b>The Flying King</b>\nPromotion: a piece becomes a king only if it finishes its turn on the opponent's back row - if it jumps through the back row and lands elsewhere, it stays a regular piece. Long-Range Flight: a king can slide any number of empty squares along a diagonal line. Long-Range Jumps: a king can capture an enemy piece from a distance, fly over it, and choose which empty square to land on behind it.\n\n<b>Winning the Game</b>\nElimination or Block: capturing all opposing pieces, or leaving your opponent with no legal moves."
  rows: 10
  columns: 10
  pieceRowsPerSide: 4
  movementScheme: 0
  piecesOnAllSquares: 0
  leaveBackRowEmpty: 0
  flyingKings: 1
  menCaptureBackward: 1
  menCannotCaptureKings: 0
  mustCaptureMaximum: 1
  preferKingMover: 0
  preferKingCaptures: 0
  preferEarlierKingCapture: 0
  midChainPromotionRule: 0
  deferCaptureRemoval: 1
  forbidImmediateReversal: 0
  noProgressMoveLimit: 25
  singleManLosesToKing: 0
